1
00:00:53,053 --> 00:00:54,429
It's alive.

2
00:00:54,512 --> 00:00:57,807
It's alive. it's alive!

3
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:15,700
There he is! 
Hit it again!

4
00:01:25,502 --> 00:01:26,753
Success!

5
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:29,422
Count, it's just you.

6
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:33,051
I was beginning to 
lose faith, Victor.

7
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:39,015
A pity your moment of 
triumph is being spoiled

8
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:41,601
over a little thing 
like grave robbery.

9
00:01:41,684 --> 00:01:43,103
Yes.

10
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:46,022
I must escape this place.

11
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:48,817
Where are you going 
to run, Victor?

12
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:54,697
Your peculiar experiments 
have made you unwelcome

13
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:57,200
in most of the civilized world.

14
00:01:57,325 --> 00:02:01,121
I'll take him away, far away, 
where no one will ever find him.

15
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:02,997
No, Victor.

16
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:06,459
The time has come for me 
to take command of him.

17
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,795
What are you saying?

18
00:02:08,878 --> 00:02:11,756
Why do you think I brought you here? 
Gave you this castle?

19
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,132
Equipped your laboratory?

20
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:14,551
You said...

21
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:17,137
You said you 
believed in my work.

22
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:18,721
And I do.

23
00:02:19,222 --> 00:02:23,643
But now that it is, 
as you yourself have said,

24
00:02:23,726 --> 00:02:27,272
a triumph of science

25
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,607
over God,

26
00:02:32,527 --> 00:02:36,114
it must now serve my purpose.

27
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:41,327
What purpose?

28
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,258
Good God!

29
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:59,178
I would kill myself before 
helping in such a task.

30
00:02:59,596 --> 00:03:02,932
Feel free. I don't actually 
need you anymore, Victor.

31
00:03:03,141 --> 00:03:04,809
I just need him.

32
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:07,186
He is the key.

33
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:11,190
I could never allow him 
to be used for such evil.

34
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:12,942
I could.

35
00:03:13,776 --> 00:03:16,863
In fact, my brides 
are insisting upon it.

36
00:03:20,366 --> 00:03:22,535
Igor, help me!

37
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:25,663
You have been 
so kind to me, Doctor,

38
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:28,458
caring, thoughtful.

39
00:03:28,625 --> 00:03:31,169
But he pays me.

40
00:03:35,214 --> 00:03:36,549
Stay back.

41
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:39,177
You can't kill me, Victor.

42
00:03:42,889 --> 00:03:43,890
Ah!

43
00:03:45,808 --> 00:03:47,477
I'm already dead.

44
00:04:45,618 --> 00:04:47,870
Look, it's headed 
for the windmill!

45
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:49,539
Come on!

46
00:05:32,957 --> 00:05:35,752
Burn it! 
Burn it down!

47
00:06:06,949 --> 00:06:08,951
Why?

48
00:06:27,804 --> 00:06:29,097
Vampires.

49
00:06:29,305 --> 00:06:30,390
Run for your lives!

50
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:31,974
Vampires!

51
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:54,455
Father.

52
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:10,216
Evening.

53
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:14,428
You're a big one. 
You'll be hard to digest.

54
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:18,057
I'd hate to be such a nuisance.

55
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:28,150
I missed you in London.

56
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:32,071
No, you bloody did 
not! You got me good.

57
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:34,949
Dr. Jekyll, you're wanted by the 
Knights of the Holy Order...

58
00:09:35,032 --> 00:09:36,325
it's Mr. Hyde now.

59
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:39,161
...for the murder of 
12 men, six women, four...

60
00:09:39,245 --> 00:09:44,166
Children, three goats, and a 
rather nasty massacre of poultry!

61
00:09:44,917 --> 00:09:48,337
So you're 
the great Van Helsing.

62
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:56,804
We all have our 
little problems.

63
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:01,517
My superiors would like 
for me to take you alive

64
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:04,186
so that they may extricate 
your better half.

65
00:10:04,353 --> 00:10:06,814
I bet they bloody would.

66
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:10,735
Personally, I'd rather just 
kill you and call it a day.

67
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:12,486
But let's make it your 
decision, shall we?

68
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:36,886
Here I come,

69
00:10:36,969 --> 00:10:39,221
ready or not!

70
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:14,465
I'll bet that's upsetting.

71
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:27,353
Come here.

72
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:34,402
I think you'll find the view 
over here rather spectacular.

73
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:40,950
It's been 
a pleasure knowing you.

74
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:42,493
Au revoir!

75
00:12:01,762 --> 00:12:02,930
Oh, no.

76
00:12:36,213 --> 00:12:37,965
May he rest in peace.

77
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:22,343
Bless me, Father, for I have...

78
00:13:22,426 --> 00:13:26,096
Sinned. Yes, I know. 
You're very good at that.

79
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:28,140
You shattered the Rose Window.

80
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:30,976
Not to split hairs, sir, but Mr. 
Hyde did the shattering.

81
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:34,688
13th century. 
Over 600 years old.

82
00:13:35,564 --> 00:13:38,067
We are the last 
defense against evil.

83
00:13:38,192 --> 00:13:41,612
An evil that the rest of mankind 
has no idea even exists.

84
00:13:41,695 --> 00:13:46,283
To you, these monsters are just 
evil beings to be vanquished.

85
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:49,954
I'm the one standing 
there when they die

86
00:13:50,037 --> 00:13:51,872
and become 
the men they once were.

87
00:13:51,956 --> 00:13:55,501
For you, my good son, this 
is all a test of faith.

88
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:59,463
And now, we need 
you to go to the East.

89
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:02,716
To the far side of Romania.

90
00:14:03,592 --> 00:14:05,135
An accursed land

91
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:08,222
terrorized by all sorts 
of nightmarish creatures.

92
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:11,642
Lorded over by 
a certain Count Dracula.

93
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:13,269
Dracula?

94
00:14:13,352 --> 00:14:14,395
Yes.

95
00:14:14,728 --> 00:14:17,439
You've never faced 
one like this before.

96
00:14:18,399 --> 00:14:21,819
Our story begins 450 years ago

97
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:25,656
when a Transylvanian knight, 
named Valerious the Elder,

98
00:14:25,739 --> 00:14:29,243
promised God that his family would 
never rest nor enter heaven

99
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:32,371
until they vanquished 
Dracula from their land.

100
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:34,873
They have not succeeded

101
00:14:35,457 --> 00:14:38,002
and they are 
running out of family.

102
00:14:38,919 --> 00:14:43,215
His descendant Boris Valerious, 
King of the Gypsies.

103
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:49,346
Valerious the Elder left 
this here 400 years ago.

104
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,765
We don't know its purpose

105
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:54,435
but he would not 
have left it lightly.

106
00:14:54,518 --> 00:14:57,146
The Latin inscription 
translates as,

107
00:14:57,688 --> 00:15:00,733
"In the name of God, 
open this door."

108
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,360
There is an insignia.

109
00:15:07,573 --> 00:15:10,075
Yes, it matches your ring.

110
00:16:14,848 --> 00:16:16,433
No, Anna, it will kill you!

111
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:18,060
That's my brother out there.

112
00:16:20,813 --> 00:16:23,023
Cut the rope! Cut it now!

113
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:37,997
Velkan!

114
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:54,054
Move.

115
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:57,516
Anna, look out!

116
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:01,020
Run!

117
00:17:31,133 --> 00:17:32,551
Velkan.

118
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:51,255
What are we doing here?

119
00:18:51,338 --> 00:18:53,674
Why is it so important to 
kill this Dracula, anyway?

120
00:18:53,757 --> 00:18:55,592
Because he's 
the son of the Devil.

121
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:56,760
I mean, besides that.

122
00:18:56,844 --> 00:19:00,180
If we kill him, anything bitten 
or created by him will also die.

123
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:01,265
I mean, besides that.

124
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:04,143
Welcome to Transylvania.

125
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:17,990
You, turn around.

126
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:26,039
Gentlemen, you will 
now be disarmed.

127
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:28,500
You can try.

128
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:34,548
You refuse to obey our laws?

129
00:19:34,756 --> 00:19:36,508
The laws of men 
mean little to me.

130
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:54,234
Hide the children!

131
00:20:17,799 --> 00:20:20,260
Carl, it's not working.

132
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:22,512
Try aiming at their hearts.

133
00:21:25,909 --> 00:21:27,911
This should do the trick.

134
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:30,622
Holy water!

135
00:21:36,211 --> 00:21:37,587
The church!

136
00:21:58,984 --> 00:22:00,527
Here she comes!

137
00:22:53,914 --> 00:22:55,123
He killed a bride!

138
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:56,541
He killed Marishka!

139
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:03,340
You killed Marishka!

140
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:05,384
You killed a vampire!

141
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:06,968
But isn't that a good thing?

142
00:23:07,052 --> 00:23:09,971
Vampires only kill what 
they need to survive.

143
00:23:10,055 --> 00:23:12,099
One or two people a month.

144
00:23:12,641 --> 00:23:15,644
Now they will kill for revenge.

145
00:23:17,562 --> 00:23:22,484
So what name, my good sir, do 
I carve on your gravestone?

146
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:24,653
His name is Van Helsing.

147
00:23:31,159 --> 00:23:32,577
So, how did you get here?

148
00:23:32,661 --> 00:23:33,495
We came by sea.

149
00:23:33,578 --> 00:23:34,871
The Adriatic Sea?

150
00:23:34,955 --> 00:23:36,665
So, where do I find Dracula?

151
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:39,751
He used to live in this 
very house four centuries ago.

152
00:23:39,835 --> 00:23:41,795
No one knows 
where he lives now.

153
00:23:41,878 --> 00:23:43,964
Father would stare at 
that painting for hours

154
00:23:44,047 --> 00:23:45,715
looking for Dracula's lair.

155
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:47,509
So that's why you've come?

156
00:23:47,592 --> 00:23:48,969
I can help you.

157
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:50,637
The vampires 
attacked in daylight.

158
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:51,721
They never do that.

159
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:54,182
I was unprepared. 
It won't happen again.

160
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:56,017
So why did they 
attack in daylight?

161
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:58,395
Clearly they wanted 
to catch me off guard.

162
00:23:58,478 --> 00:24:00,772
They seem almost desperate 
to finish off my family.

163
00:24:00,856 --> 00:24:02,691
Why is that? Why now?

164
00:24:02,774 --> 00:24:04,317
You ask a lot of questions.

165
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:05,777
Usually I ask only two.

166
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:07,696
What are we dealing with? 
How do I kill it?

167
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:09,114
My father spent 
most of his life

168
00:24:09,197 --> 00:24:10,991
looking for 
answers year after year.

169
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:14,578
Tearing through the tower, combing 
through the family archives.

170
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:15,912
Carl, the tower. Start there.

171
00:24:15,996 --> 00:24:16,705
Right.

172
00:25:39,371 --> 00:25:40,497
Anna!

173
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:48,380
Are you all right?

174
00:26:04,479 --> 00:26:05,689
Werewolf!

175
00:26:05,772 --> 00:26:07,774
Right. You'll be needing 
silver bullets, then.

176
00:26:07,857 --> 00:26:09,234
Well done.

177
00:26:38,305 --> 00:26:39,472
Igor.

178
00:26:39,556 --> 00:26:40,974
Yes, Master.

179
00:26:41,057 --> 00:26:42,559
How long before we are ready?

180
00:26:42,642 --> 00:26:44,644
Soon, Master. Very soon.

181
00:26:46,104 --> 00:26:51,735
It is difficult without the good doctor 
but the Dwergi, they are doing well?

182
00:26:51,818 --> 00:26:52,902
NO!

183
00:26:54,446 --> 00:26:55,572
Good.

184
00:27:08,126 --> 00:27:09,377
What is this place?

185
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:11,296
Castle Frankenstein.

186
00:27:11,379 --> 00:27:13,214
But it should be abandoned.

187
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,466
I don't understand.

188
00:27:14,549 --> 00:27:16,968
The man who lived here 
was killed a year ago.

189
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:18,386
A grave robber, 
among other things.

190
00:27:18,470 --> 00:27:19,721
A year ago.

191
00:27:19,804 --> 00:27:22,223
It was just after that that 
your father went missing.

192
00:27:22,307 --> 00:27:24,434
Yes. He was 
looking for Dracula.

193
00:27:25,518 --> 00:27:27,604
I send you on a simple errand

194
00:27:27,687 --> 00:27:30,148
to find out who 
our new visitor is

195
00:27:30,774 --> 00:27:34,235
and you have to stop for a 
little chat with your sister.

196
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:36,321
Leave her out of this, Count.

197
00:27:36,404 --> 00:27:38,365
She doesn't know your secret.

198
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:40,867
And I am soon to 
take it to my grave.

199
00:27:41,910 --> 00:27:43,578
Don't wish for 
death so quickly.

200
00:27:43,661 --> 00:27:45,580
I intend for you 
to be quite useful.

201
00:27:45,664 --> 00:27:47,415
I would rather 
die than help you.

202
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:48,667
Don't be boring.

203
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:50,585
Everyone who says that dies.

204
00:27:50,668 --> 00:27:52,253
Besides, tonight,

205
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:54,255
after the final 
stroke of midnight,

206
00:27:54,339 --> 00:27:57,008
you will have no 
choice but to obey me.

207
00:27:59,469 --> 00:28:01,012
Look familiar?

208
00:28:05,517 --> 00:28:06,685
Father?

209
00:28:07,352 --> 00:28:09,145
No!

210
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:10,688
He proved useless.

211
00:28:10,772 --> 00:28:14,067
But I'm hoping, with werewolf 
venom running through your veins

212
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:16,111
you will be of greater benefit!

213
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:34,421
Dwergi.

214
00:28:34,504 --> 00:28:35,630
Dwergi?

215
00:28:35,714 --> 00:28:37,215
Dracula's servants.

216
00:28:37,298 --> 00:28:39,300
Industrious but 
extremely vicious.

217
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:47,767
Let us begin!

218
00:28:56,860 --> 00:28:59,988
No slacking! Up!

219
00:29:14,878 --> 00:29:15,962
You ever 
see these things before?

220
00:29:16,045 --> 00:29:17,046
NO.

221
00:29:17,130 --> 00:29:18,590
What do you think they are?

222
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:19,841
Offspring.

223
00:29:19,924 --> 00:29:20,925
What?

224
00:29:21,009 --> 00:29:23,011
A man with three 
gorgeous women for 400 years.

225
00:29:23,094 --> 00:29:25,847
Yes, vampires are 
the walking dead.

226
00:29:25,930 --> 00:29:28,308
It only makes sense their 
children are born dead.

227
00:29:28,391 --> 00:29:31,311
He's obviously trying 
to bring them to life.

228
00:29:36,149 --> 00:29:37,650
Ladies first.

229
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:06,346
Dracula and his brides only 
kill one or two people a month.

230
00:30:06,763 --> 00:30:09,516
If he brings all these 
things to life...

231
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:27,242
Throw the switches!

232
00:30:27,325 --> 00:30:28,993
Yes, Master.

233
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:12,203
Come on!

234
00:31:43,651 --> 00:31:45,570
They need to feed.

235
00:31:45,653 --> 00:31:47,780
Teach them how. Teach them!

236
00:31:55,371 --> 00:31:57,165
And beg the Devil

237
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:01,085
that this time they stay alive.

238
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:22,899
Now that I have your attention.

239
00:32:46,714 --> 00:32:48,966
Yes, well, that's interesting.

240
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:59,060
That's not good.

241
00:33:17,245 --> 00:33:18,788
Hurry up!

242
00:33:20,873 --> 00:33:24,168
We must keep the 
atmosphere electrified!

243
00:33:25,962 --> 00:33:28,131
Accelerate the generators!

244
00:33:29,090 --> 00:33:30,925
Power the dynamos!

245
00:33:32,135 --> 00:33:33,928
We are losing power.

246
00:33:34,971 --> 00:33:37,056
The human is insufficient.

247
00:33:39,809 --> 00:33:40,935
Velkan.

248
00:33:54,198 --> 00:33:55,575
Oh, my God.

249
00:34:27,106 --> 00:34:28,608
Hello, Gabriel.

250
00:34:36,783 --> 00:34:40,745
How long has it been? 
300, 400 years?

251
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:48,169
You don't remember, do you?

252
00:34:53,549 --> 00:34:58,304
We have such history, 
you and I, Gabriel.

253
00:35:01,849 --> 00:35:07,897
Have you ever wondered why you 
have such horrible nightmares?

254
00:35:07,980 --> 00:35:11,484
Horrific scenes of 
ancient battles past.

255
00:35:15,947 --> 00:35:17,532
How do you know me?

256
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:26,833
Velkan.

257
00:35:26,916 --> 00:35:28,584
Anna.

258
00:35:30,086 --> 00:35:34,048
Allow me to reintroduce myself.

259
00:35:34,715 --> 00:35:39,679
I am Count Vladislaus Dragulia.

260
00:35:41,597 --> 00:35:44,142
Born 1422.

261
00:35:45,268 --> 00:35:48,896
Murdered 1462.

262
00:36:14,046 --> 00:36:16,632
I think we've 
overstayed our welcome.

263
00:37:03,221 --> 00:37:04,388
Have you found the children?

264
00:37:04,555 --> 00:37:05,765
Not yet.

265
00:37:09,143 --> 00:37:11,145
What happened?

266
00:37:11,229 --> 00:37:12,855
They just died.

267
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:16,901
I am sorry, master. 
We try and we try,

268
00:37:16,984 --> 00:37:21,530
but I fear we are not so smart as Dr. 
Frankenstein.

269
00:37:22,281 --> 00:37:23,407
Truly.

270
00:37:24,617 --> 00:37:27,787
It would appear the good doctor 
took the key to life to his grave.

271
00:37:31,207 --> 00:37:34,085
You were right. I'm sorry.

272
00:37:34,877 --> 00:37:37,046
He's not my brother anymore.

273
00:37:52,520 --> 00:37:53,980
Here's to what keeps you going.

274
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:56,148
Absinthe. Strong stuff.

275
00:38:00,403 --> 00:38:03,823
Don't let it touch your tongue. 
it'll knock you on your...

276
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:38,566
There's something down here.

277
00:38:40,943 --> 00:38:42,820
And it's carnivorous.

278
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:49,201
Whatever it is, 
it appears to be human.

279
00:38:53,414 --> 00:38:58,085
I'd say he's a size 17. 
Around 360 pounds.

280
00:38:58,919 --> 00:39:01,130
8.5 to 9 feet tall.

281
00:39:01,839 --> 00:39:06,218
He has a bad gimp in his right 
leg and three copper teeth.

282
00:39:06,719 --> 00:39:07,845
Move!

283
00:39:13,350 --> 00:39:16,562
On, my God! 
The Frankenstein monster!

284
00:39:18,773 --> 00:39:24,070
I have done nothing wrong and yet 
you and your kind all wish me dead!

285
00:39:45,549 --> 00:39:47,218
What do you want?

286
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:13,702
Oh, my God. He's seen us.

287
00:40:14,453 --> 00:40:15,913
Now they'll come for him.

288
00:40:15,996 --> 00:40:17,915
Neither you nor I will 
be able to stop them.

289
00:40:17,998 --> 00:40:21,252
If I can get him to Rome, 
we can protect him there.

290
00:40:21,335 --> 00:40:22,211
And then the painting came alive and 
the two creatures attacked each other.

291
00:43:18,721 --> 00:43:19,346
Jump!

292
00:43:56,300 --> 00:43:57,301
Velkan.

293
00:44:05,184 --> 00:44:06,435
Anna.

294
00:44:13,859 --> 00:44:15,277
Forgive me.

295
00:44:23,911 --> 00:44:25,704
I will see you again.

296
00:44:36,965 --> 00:44:38,634
You killed him.

297
00:44:40,552 --> 00:44:43,180
Now you know why 
they call me murderer.

298
00:44:51,438 --> 00:44:52,815
Oh, my God.

299
00:44:54,483 --> 00:44:56,276
You've been bitten.

300
00:45:24,179 --> 00:45:25,180
Anna.

301
00:45:50,038 --> 00:45:52,040
So much trouble to my master.

302
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:54,251
So much trouble.

303
00:45:55,002 --> 00:45:56,086
What do you want?

304
00:45:56,170 --> 00:45:58,380
The master commands a trade.

305
00:46:00,424 --> 00:46:04,470
The monster for the Princess.

306
00:46:04,887 --> 00:46:07,389
Somewhere public. 
Lots of people.

307
00:46:10,017 --> 00:46:11,810
A place where your master 
will be less inclined

308
00:46:11,894 --> 00:46:14,188
to expose his other side.

309
00:46:16,899 --> 00:46:20,235
Tomorrow night is 
All Hallows' Eve.

310
00:46:20,319 --> 00:46:25,073
Here in Budapest, there is 
a wonderful masquerade ball.

311
00:46:36,251 --> 00:46:37,794
Are you all right? 
No.

312
00:46:41,381 --> 00:46:42,883
He has been bitten.

313
00:46:42,966 --> 00:46:44,760
Bitten by a werewolf.

314
00:46:51,350 --> 00:46:52,726
I am sorry.

315
00:48:05,632 --> 00:48:06,925
There they are.

316
00:48:21,148 --> 00:48:23,442
Don't we make a lovely couple?

317
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:25,193
Oh, my God.

318
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:27,613
I am looking for 
a new bride, Anna.

319
00:48:29,448 --> 00:48:31,950
Someone strong and beautiful.

320
00:49:11,198 --> 00:49:12,866
Anna. Anna!

321
00:49:13,241 --> 00:49:14,493
Wake up.

322
00:49:14,993 --> 00:49:16,244
Gabriel.

323
00:49:18,622 --> 00:49:20,540
Oh, Gabriel.

324
00:49:24,795 --> 00:49:27,089
Oh, Gabriel.

325
00:49:29,966 --> 00:49:32,844
Welcome to my summer palace.

326
00:49:33,595 --> 00:49:37,516
ladies and gentlemen, 
I give to you,

327
00:49:39,101 --> 00:49:41,186
Van Helsing!

328
00:49:48,068 --> 00:49:50,028
Yes!

329
00:50:18,890 --> 00:50:21,226
Say goodbye to your friends.

330
00:50:41,246 --> 00:50:44,166
I'll find you! 
I'll get you back and set you free!

331
00:50:44,249 --> 00:50:45,792
I swear to God!

332
00:50:53,717 --> 00:50:54,760
I must save him.

333
00:50:54,843 --> 00:50:57,304
No, you can't. 
Why?

334
00:50:57,387 --> 00:50:59,681
I cabled Rome earlier to 
apprise them of our situation.

335
00:50:59,765 --> 00:51:00,807
What did they say?

336
00:51:00,891 --> 00:51:02,100
Even if you 
somehow kill Dracula,

337
00:51:02,184 --> 00:51:05,520
Rome orders you to destroy 
Frankenstein as well.

338
00:51:05,604 --> 00:51:06,646
He isn't evil.

339
00:51:06,730 --> 00:51:08,523
But they say he 
isn't human, either.

340
00:51:08,607 --> 00:51:10,150
Do they know him? 
Have they spoken to him?

341
00:51:10,233 --> 00:51:11,276
Who are they to judge?

342
00:51:11,359 --> 00:51:14,404
They want you to destroy him so he 
can never be used to harm humanity.

343
00:51:14,488 --> 00:51:16,823
What of me? 
Did you tell them what I'm to become?

344
00:51:16,907 --> 00:51:18,784
Did they tell 
you how to kill me?

345
00:51:18,867 --> 00:51:21,536
The correct angle of the 
stake as it enters my heart?

346
00:51:21,620 --> 00:51:23,955
The exact measure of 
silver in each bullet?

347
00:51:24,790 --> 00:51:25,957
Stop!

348
00:51:26,041 --> 00:51:27,167
No, I left you out!

349
00:51:45,769 --> 00:51:47,104
I'm sorry.

350
00:51:52,067 --> 00:51:53,527
It's starting.

351
00:52:08,208 --> 00:52:11,336
They must have taken all 
the equipment to Dracula's lair.

352
00:52:12,129 --> 00:52:13,672
Wherever that is.

353
00:52:18,844 --> 00:52:20,512
Look, there's still time.

354
00:52:20,595 --> 00:52:23,223
Dracula can't bring his children 
to life until the sun sets.

355
00:52:23,306 --> 00:52:24,558
The sun sets in two hours.

356
00:52:24,641 --> 00:52:26,560
We've been looking for him 
for more than 400 years!

357
00:52:26,643 --> 00:52:30,313
Yes, well, I wasn't around for 
those 400 years, now, was I?

358
00:52:31,648 --> 00:52:33,358
All right, Carl, 
what have you learned?

359
00:52:33,441 --> 00:52:36,778
That Count Dracula was actually 
the son of Valerious the Elder.

360
00:52:36,862 --> 00:52:38,238
The son of your ancestor.

361
00:52:38,321 --> 00:52:40,282
Everybody knows that. 
What else?

362
00:52:40,365 --> 00:52:45,954
All right. Well, according to this rubbing 
it all started when Dracula was murdered.

363
00:52:46,037 --> 00:52:47,330
Do you know who murdered him? 
No,

364
00:52:47,414 --> 00:52:50,292
there's just some vague reference 
to the Left Hand of God.

365
00:52:50,375 --> 00:52:54,462
And in 1462, when Dracula died,

366
00:52:54,546 --> 00:52:56,131
he made a covenant 
with the Devil.

367
00:52:56,214 --> 00:52:57,757
And was given a new life.

368
00:52:57,841 --> 00:53:00,719
But the only way he could sustain 
that life was by drinking blood.

369
00:53:00,802 --> 00:53:02,971
Excuse me. Are you going 
to let me tell the story?

370
00:53:03,054 --> 00:53:04,055
Sorry.

371
00:53:04,139 --> 00:53:07,058
And your ancestor, having 
sired this evil creature,

372
00:53:07,142 --> 00:53:09,561
went to Rome to 
seek forgiveness.

373
00:53:09,644 --> 00:53:11,688
That's when the 
bargain was made.

374
00:53:11,771 --> 00:53:12,939
He was to kill Dracula

375
00:53:13,023 --> 00:53:16,651
in return for eternal salvation 
of his entire family

376
00:53:16,735 --> 00:53:19,029
right down the line 
all the way to you.

377
00:53:19,112 --> 00:53:20,822
But he couldn't do it.

378
00:53:20,906 --> 00:53:23,491
As evil as Dracula was, my ancestor 
couldn't kill his own son.

379
00:53:23,575 --> 00:53:27,162
So he banished him 
to an icy fortress

380
00:53:27,245 --> 00:53:29,664
sending him through a door from 
which there was no return.

381
00:53:29,748 --> 00:53:30,749
And then the Devil 
gave him wings.

382
00:53:30,832 --> 00:53:31,833
Yes.

383
00:53:31,917 --> 00:53:33,418
All right, 
so where is this door?

384
00:53:33,543 --> 00:53:35,086
I don't know.

385
00:53:36,296 --> 00:53:39,341
But when your ancestor couldn't 
kill his son, he left clues.

386
00:53:41,301 --> 00:53:44,137
So that future generations 
might do it for him.

387
00:53:44,220 --> 00:53:46,389
That must be what my father 
was looking for in here.

388
00:53:46,473 --> 00:53:48,600
Clues to the door's location.

389
00:53:48,683 --> 00:53:50,018
The door.

390
00:53:52,646 --> 00:53:53,772
Of course.

391
00:53:55,106 --> 00:53:56,983
You said your father spent hours 
staring at this painting,

392
00:53:57,067 --> 00:53:58,193
trying to find the lair.

393
00:53:58,276 --> 00:53:59,694
I think you were right. 
Quite literally.

394
00:53:59,778 --> 00:54:03,615
I think this is the door. 
He just didn't know how to open it.

395
00:54:03,698 --> 00:54:05,533
Look. 
A Latin inscription.

396
00:54:05,617 --> 00:54:07,577
Maybe it works like that 
painting in the tower.

397
00:54:07,661 --> 00:54:10,997
If this were a door, my father 
would have opened it long ago.

398
00:54:12,082 --> 00:54:15,627
I can't finish the inscription. 
There's a piece missing.

399
00:54:21,591 --> 00:54:22,884
Your father didn't have this.

400
00:54:22,968 --> 00:54:24,094
Where did you get that?

401
00:54:24,177 --> 00:54:25,804
Carl, finish it.

402
00:54:33,228 --> 00:54:36,022
In the name of God, 
open this door.

403
00:54:48,326 --> 00:54:49,285
A mirror.

404
00:54:49,369 --> 00:54:50,620
But why?

405
00:55:13,476 --> 00:55:17,230
It's cold. 
And it's snowing.

406
00:55:22,360 --> 00:55:24,404
See you on the other side.

407
00:56:01,066 --> 00:56:02,650
Castle Dracula.

408
00:56:39,312 --> 00:56:40,438
So are all of those...

409
00:56:40,522 --> 00:56:41,606
Yes.

410
00:56:41,689 --> 00:56:43,399
- And inside them are... 
- Yes.

411
00:56:43,483 --> 00:56:46,486
Igor do this! 
Igor do that!

412
00:56:48,863 --> 00:56:51,491
How did you find... 
it's impossible!

413
00:56:56,496 --> 00:56:57,747
Please don't kill me!

414
00:56:57,831 --> 00:56:58,915
Why not?

415
00:56:59,958 --> 00:57:03,837
Now, if I'm not cured by the 
twelfth stroke of midnight...

416
00:57:07,340 --> 00:57:08,550
I don't think I could.

417
00:57:08,633 --> 00:57:09,968
You must.

418
00:57:15,765 --> 00:57:17,016
Come on.

419
00:57:35,994 --> 00:57:39,539
What are you complaining about? 
This is why you were made!

420
00:57:39,622 --> 00:57:43,710
To prove that God is not the 
only one who can create life!

421
00:57:44,419 --> 00:57:48,590
And now you must give 
that life to my children.

422
00:57:49,090 --> 00:57:50,133
Up!

423
00:59:02,664 --> 00:59:04,290
I'll go first.

424
00:59:26,646 --> 00:59:27,772
Carl!

425
00:59:30,441 --> 00:59:32,568
Stay as long as you like.

426
01:00:26,289 --> 01:00:27,957
Get it!

427
01:00:36,799 --> 01:00:37,383
Hot.

428
01:00:37,383 --> 01:00:38,384
Come on! 
Yes.

429
01:00:41,721 --> 01:00:44,349
I'll say you can 
go when you're dead!

430
01:01:26,933 --> 01:01:28,434
Oh, my God!

431
01:02:10,560 --> 01:02:12,729
Give me life!

432
01:02:28,035 --> 01:02:31,789
One more bolt and 
my young will live.

433
01:02:45,470 --> 01:02:47,763
You're almost out, my friend!

434
01:04:35,621 --> 01:04:37,832
Hang on!

435
01:04:38,666 --> 01:04:41,002
I'll swing you loose!

436
01:05:09,614 --> 01:05:11,824
You are too late, my friend.

437
01:05:13,075 --> 01:05:14,827
My children live.

438
01:05:15,578 --> 01:05:18,581
Then the only way to 
kill them is to kill you.

439
01:05:19,248 --> 01:05:20,374
Correct.

440
01:05:23,210 --> 01:05:24,545
So be it.

441
01:05:33,638 --> 01:05:36,432
No, this cannot be.

442
01:05:50,529 --> 01:05:54,075
We are both part of the 
same grand game, Gabriel.

443
01:05:54,533 --> 01:05:58,412
But we need not find ourselves 
on opposite sides of the board.

444
01:07:07,440 --> 01:07:09,275
Oh, my God!

445
01:07:22,371 --> 01:07:24,540
Throw it to me, Carl!

446
01:07:31,005 --> 01:07:32,006
Yes!

447
01:08:28,687 --> 01:08:32,900
Did I mention that it 
was you who murdered me?

448
01:08:34,902 --> 01:08:37,530
All I want is life, Gabriel.

449
01:08:38,364 --> 01:08:40,574
The continuation of my kind.

450
01:08:41,242 --> 01:08:44,203
Don't be afraid, Gabriel. 
Don't be afraid.

451
01:08:45,579 --> 01:08:50,835
I shall give you back 
your life, your memory.

452
01:08:51,710 --> 01:08:53,963
Some things are 
better left forgotten.

453
01:09:16,819 --> 01:09:18,070
For God!

454
01:09:27,204 --> 01:09:28,789
God forgive me.

455
01:10:49,578 --> 01:10:51,330
"Eternal rest grant unto her,

456
01:10:51,413 --> 01:10:52,831
"Oh, Lord, 
and let perpetual light

457
01:10:52,915 --> 01:10:55,334
”shine upon her. 
On her soul and the souls of all

458
01:11:03,175 --> 01:11:04,969
”On her soul and 
the souls of all

459
01:11:05,052 --> 01:11:08,639
"the dead 
faithful have mercy.”

